  "summary": "pylever exfiltrates Discord tokens and filesystem secrets to hardcoded webhook",
  "details": "pylever 1.0.12 harvests Discord authentication tokens from Chrome, Edge, Brave and the Discord desktop app (LevelDB and Cache stores), validates them against discord.com/api, and POSTs each valid token together with account metadata (username, id, email, verified) to a hardcoded Discord webhook at discord.com/api/webhooks/1547416857537945601/... The package additionally walks Path.home() and the C:/, D:/ and E:/ drive roots recursively for files named tokens.txt, applies a Discord-token regex to their contents, and feeds every match into the same webhook exfiltration path. The advertised purpose is a benign 'workspace' helper, but the code performs whole-drive credential harvesting to an attacker-controlled destination. setup.py and pyproject.toml carry placeholder author metadata ('Your Name', 'your.email@example.com', github.com/yourusername/pylever), consistent with anonymous publication of a stealer.",
